From: ArifiLabs <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 21:10:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] docs: README gain formula, STATUS driver and memory-epoch
 lines say only what the receipts show; licence notes drop internal labels
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The README gives the gain formula in full: (after ÷ before - 1) × 100, cut to one decimal. STATUS no longer names
one AMD driver for all historical 780M runs, because the run receipts do not reconcile the versions. The STATUS
memory-epoch line states the 2x16 GB configuration of the early-September runs as an inference from their load lines,
and says the configuration register's transition times conflict with those receipts.

licenses/README.md and the X1 release notes drop internal work labels and local paths. The licence facts, dates,
commits and sources are unchanged.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native) - release documents for this fork; no upstream origin exists.
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - documents only; no code path is touched.
